    (created-at, consent flag, schema version) is a migration against data already in real browsers.
  - [3mComplexity:[0m trivial.

  [1mB. ES modules + versioned JSON envelope.[0m Switch [38;5;153mindex.html[39m to [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m; [38;5;153mapp.js[39m does [38;5;153mimport
[39m  [38;5;153m{ getUserId } from "./src/identity.js"[39m. Stores [38;5;153m{"v":1,"userId":"…","createdAt":"…"}[39m.
  - [3mBuys:[0m a real import graph, no globals, and future forms declare their dependency instead of assuming a script tag
    ran first. Directly importable by a test runner later.
  - [3mCosts:[0m module scripts are blocked over [38;5;153mfile://[39m by CORS — you'd need to serve the page over http to open it at all.
    For a fixture that's currently double-clickable, that's a genuine regression. Module scope also un-globals [38;5;153mlogin[39m and
    [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m, which nothing depends on today but would surprise anyone poking at the console.
  - [3mComplexity:[0m moderate.

  [1mC. Global script + versioned JSON envelope[0m — [3mrecommended.[0m A's loading model, B's storage model.
  - [3mBuys:[0m nothing about how the page loads changes, so [38;5;153mfile://[39m keeps working and the new module reads like the code
    already here. The envelope costs ~3 extra lines now and means the next field you need is an additive change, not a
    migration — which matters precisely because you said other forms are coming.
  - [3mCosts:[0m still globals and still load-order-sensitive. You'd pay B's conversion later if you ever adopt a bundler —
    but that conversion is mechanical, and the stored format survives it untouched.
  - [3mComplexity:[0m trivial.

  [1mWhy C over B:[0m the module-system upgrade is cheap to do later and breaks nothing when you do; the storage format is the
  opposite. Spend the care on the thing that's expensive to change. [1mWhy C over A:[0m three lines now against a data
  migration later, on the strength of your own "other forms will need it."

